            <ArticleTitle>O2 activation at a trispyrazolylborato nickel(ii) malonato complex.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16792-16795</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7dt04056c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To support mechanistic inferences made for an iron-based dioxygenase model, a nickel analogue, i.e. a TpNi-malonate (1) was prepared. 1 proved to represent a rare case of a nickel complex reacting with O2 in a controlled manner - mechanistically different from the iron case - and leads to hydroxylation of the malonate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
